# Cloudflare Pages headers. Copied verbatim into dist/ by site/build.mjs, and
# applied by e2e/server.mjs so the e2e gate exercises this exact policy.
#
# Why the CSP is repeated per-path instead of set once under /*:
# Pages' merge behaviour for a header defined by BOTH /* and a more specific
# rule is not something this project can verify locally (combine vs override).
# Writing the complete policy on every path makes the result correct under
# either interpretation: no path can end up with a partial CSP, and /embed/*
# cannot inherit a frame restriction. The cost is repetition; the benefit is
# that the deployed policy is not a guess. e2e/tests/security.spec.ts asserts
# both the full policy and the embed exception.
#
# CSP trade-offs, stated honestly:
#  - 'unsafe-inline' in script-src is unavoidable: big-board.html is a frozen
#    single file whose whole app is one inline <script>, and site/'s shells
#    boot from an inline module script. Nonces need a per-request server
#    (none by design); hashing a 3000-line block that changes on most edits is
#    brittle. The host allowlist still blocks script from unknown origins,
#    which is the realistic attack.
#  - 'unsafe-inline' in style-src is required by inline style= attributes
#    carrying per-item accent colors.
#  - cdn.jsdelivr.net serves SortableJS + PapaParse, used ONLY by the frozen
#    big-board.html; the generic app has zero runtime deps. (An earlier draft
#    guessed cdnjs here — the e2e CSP test caught it before it shipped.)
#  - blob:/data: in img-src cover the canvas PNG export path.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Frame protection on every surface EXCEPT /embed/*, which exists to be
